prns for Debian
===============

prnsd is Prns's Reticulum daemon. This package starts it in every user's
session (systemd user service prnsd.service) as the machine's Reticulum
shared instance, unless one already runs (rnsd, or another prnsd): then it
stays off and apps use that one.

    systemctl --user status prnsd
    journalctl --user -u prnsd
    prnsd logs | prnsd restart | prnsd stop

Its configuration is ~/.reticulum/config, written on the first start with
the automatic interfaces on; add TCP interfaces there to reach hubs.

This build is headless (no tray). It's a packaging of upstream Prns
(https://github.com/KenAKAFrosty/Prns) for retifs' testers, from the fork
https://github.com/vooteleaer/Prns (branch retifs), until Prns publishes
packages of its own.
